<title>USA: Raychem books $23 mln Q1 pretax gain.</title>
<headline>Raychem books $23 mln Q1 pretax gain.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raychem Corp on Friday said it sold a portfolio of patents and related intellectual property to Medtronic Inc.</p>
<p>The company said the sale resulted in a fiscal first quarter pretax gain of approximately $23 million.</p>
<p>The portfolio is comprised primarily of patents and patent applications relating to the use of nickel titanium for medical applications.</p>
</text>
